      "trigger": "A SYNTHETIC local corpus raises on the first retrieve for one (question_id,repeat,mode), then returns canonical fixture cards on a later call. Run paired cells T→TV, G→GV, or TV→T.",
      "expected": "The registered pair shares one retrieval attempt/outcome, including a failed outcome. The second group must not perform a new retrieval and selectively recover.",
      "actual": "Cache assignment occurs only after retrieve returns. A failure leaves no cache entry; second paired group calls retrieve again. T→TV and G→GV yielded first cell tested_failure with zero cards and second cell completed/publishable with cards. TV→T reversed the advantage.",
